  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancing Policy Making and Implementation Capacity in Social Protection</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The grant will support capacity development activities in three main  areas of social protection:  (i) social safety nets; (ii) active labor market policy; and (iii) pension reform.  Activities include: 1. surveys to assess the effectiveness of NGOs and CBOs in providing safety nets; 2. Developing data module to complement the national HIES to assess socioeconomic risks and responses of households 3. Tracer study on vocational and technical training graduates 4. Baseline survey on existing pension system 5. TA to MOSAL and SPC staff on SP policies, analysis, diagnosis 6. Training to support MOSAL and SPC 7. Project coordination and support activities Grant period for 2 years, from July 2006 through July 2008. To enhance the capacity of the Ministry of Social Affairs and Labor to analyze and improve implementation of social protection policies and programs.  Capacity development activities are supported in two areas of social protection: (i) social safety nets; and (ii) pension reform.</narrative>
  </description>
